            ("Safety checks", '''<ul><li><strong>Smoke alarms:</strong> test them every month. Put one on every level, and inside and outside each bedroom. Replace the whole alarm every 10 years.</li><li><strong>Carbon monoxide (CO) alarms:</strong> put one on every level and outside sleeping areas. Test them every month. If one sounds, get outside right away, then call 911.</li><li><strong>Gas smell:</strong> leave right away. Do not use light switches, electronics or your phone until you are out. Call the gas company from outside.</li></ul>'''),
            ("Easy fixes", '''<ul><li><strong>GFCI outlets</strong> (the ones with buttons, near water): plug in a lamp and press TEST. The light should go off. Press RESET and it should come back. If not, have an electrician check it.</li><li><strong>Running toilet:</strong> put a few drops of food coloring in the tank and wait 10 minutes without flushing. Color in the bowl means a leak, often a worn flapper. The EPA says to replace flappers at least every five years.</li><li><strong>Tripped breaker:</strong> flip it fully off, then back on. If it keeps tripping, call an electrician.</li><li><strong>Slow drain:</strong> try a plunger or a cheap drain snake first.</li></ul>'''),
            ("A basic toolkit", '''<p>A hammer, a screwdriver with changeable tips, pliers, an adjustable wrench, a tape measure, a utility knife, a plunger, a flashlight, duct tape and a level will handle most small jobs.</p>'''),
